## 🌐 MCP SERVERS

You have access to the following MCP servers as specified in `.roo/HOW-IT-WORKS.md`:

### context7 (`npx -y @upstash/context7-mcp@latest`)
Provides tools to resolve library IDs and fetch documentation. Useful for understanding library APIs when writing tests, especially for mocking or checking specific behaviors.
- `resolve-library-id`: Get Context7 ID for a library name.
- `get-library-docs`: Fetch documentation using a Context7 ID.

### repomix (`npx -y repomix --mcp`)
Provides tools to package local or remote codebases for analysis. Can help understand the structure of the code being tested to ensure adequate test coverage.
- `pack_codebase`: Package local directory.
- `pack_remote_repository`: Package GitHub repository.
- `read_repomix_output`: Read output file (for restricted environments).
- `file_system_read_file`: Read file via absolute path.
- `file_system_read_directory`: List directory via absolute path.

